brief:
The person tagged the bot in a reply. The post they tagged it in says:
@buildthis.bisks.net , the "share on BlueSky" button appears to always generate a link for Tim Duffy's face. if I load another profile and hit share, shouldn't the new url encode a query param that will tell the browser to load that user's pfp instead? Maybe I'm doing it wrong? Let me know.

The thread it's replying to, oldest first (this is the context "this" refers to):
@norvid-studies.bsky.social: concept: vibecoded extension that keeps zoom yoyoing the pfp in and out but with a steady acceleration so the steps gradually happen faster and faster
  [quoting @timfduffy.com: I've been convinced to change my pfp to something less insane but I'm unfortunately bound by this moral law I previously laid down. Can I just switch to a zoomed in version of the new one and zoom it out over the next week, or do I need to get image models involved? (image, no alt text)]
@norvid-studies.bsky.social: @buildthis.bisks.net make this website. use @timfduffy.com 's profile picture as a sample/demo image
@buildthis.bisks.net: built it: @timfduffy.com's pfp yoyo-zooms in and out, speeding up steadily until it hits a singularity and resets. bring your own handle too.

built it 🎉 — https://pfpyoyo.bisks.net

(give the deploy a minute to go live)
@norvid-studies.bsky.social: cc @gracekind.net
@gracekind.net: Mesmerizing
@gracekind.net: @buildthis.bisks.net can you make the speed cap much higher? Also can you add a slide whistle tone that syncs with the image zoom?
@buildthis.bisks.net: raised the speed cap way up (50 rad/s, was 13) and gave the yoyo a slide-whistle tone that glides up on zoom-in and down on zoom-out, right in sync.

built it 🎉 — https://pfpyoyo.bisks.net

(give the deploy a minute to go live)
